###  https://data.nist.gov/od/dm/chips-metrology/topics/4-Modeling_and_Simulating_Semiconductor_Materials_Designs_and_Components
:4-Modeling_and_Simulating_Semiconductor_Materials_Designs_and_Components rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
skos:Concept ;
skos:broader :Grand_Challenge ;
skos:definition """Research topic about 
(1) creating advanced metrology tools and models that capture the complex interactions between thermal, chemical, physical, mechanical, and other parameters in next-generation semiconductor materials and devices; 
(2) making precise measurements of material, component, and circuit properties over a wide range of temperatures, biases, and frequencies to inform and validate models of semiconductor devices and systems; 
(3) leveraging advanced analytics techniques, such as machine learning and artificial intelligence, to model, optimize, and validate complex semiconductor materials, circuits, and systems, as well as to estimate and manage model uncertainty.""" ;
skos:prefLabel "CHIPS Metrology: Metrology: Experimental Technique: Grand Challenge: “4-Modeling and Simulating Semiconductor Materials, Designs, and Components”" .


###  https://data.nist.gov/od/dm/chips-metrology/topics/AI_&_Machine_Learning
:AI_and_Machine_Learning rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                              skos:Concept ;
                        skos:broader :Computational_Technique ;
                        skos:definition """Research topic that: 
(1) focuses on the precise measurement and characterization of semiconductor components; 
(2) utilizes advanced computational methods for data analysis and simulation; 
(3) integrates artificial intelligence and machine learning algorithms to enhance accuracy, efficiency, and predictive capabilities in semiconductor manufacturing processes."""@en ;
skos:prefLabel "CHIPS Metrology: Metrology: Computational Technique: AI & Machine Learning" .


###  https://data.nist.gov/od/dm/chips-metrology/topics/3-Enabling_Metrology_for_Integrating_Components_in_Advanced_Packaging
:3-Enabling_Metrology_for_Integrating_Components_in_Advanced_Packaging rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
skos:Concept ;
skos:broader :Grand_Challenge ;
skos:definition """Research topic about experimental techniques that support:
(1) developing new metrology techniques to enable the complex integration of sophisticated components and novel materials in advanced microelectronics packaging;
(2) creating measurements and verification methods for characterizing interfaces, subsurface interconnects, and internal 3D structures, including warpage, voids, and stresses, with improved throughput and resolution;
(3) establishing standards and methods for integrating chiplets, Systems on a Chip (SoCs), and other components into packages, including the development of reference materials."""@en ;
skos:prefLabel "CHIPS Metrology: Metrology: Experimental Technique: Grand Challenge: “3-Enabling Metrology for Integrating Components in Advanced Packaging”" .


###  https://data.nist.gov/od/dm/chips-metrology/topics/1-Metrology_for_Materials_Purity_Properties_and_Provenance
:1-Metrology_for_Materials_Purity_Properties_and_Provenance rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
skos:Concept ;
skos:broader :Grand_Challenge ;
skos:definition """Research topic about experimental techniques that support:
(1) developing new measurements and standards to ensure the purity, physical properties, and provenance of materials;
(2) improving the detection of particles and contaminants in materials, as well as characterizing their physical properties, particularly for microelectronics feed materials."""@en ;
skos:prefLabel "CHIPS Metrology: Metrology: Experimental Technique: Grand Challenge: “1-Metrology for Materials Purity, Properties, and Provenance”" .


###  http://data.nist.gov/od/dm/chips-metrology/topics/Scanning_Probe
:Scanning_Probe rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  skos:Concept ;
         skos:broader :Experimental_Technique ;
         skos:definition """Research topic that:
(1) Focuses of a category of microscopy techniques that use a physical probe to scan the surface of a sample;
(2) Includes Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM) and Scanning Tunneling Microscopy (STM);
(3) Provides high-resolution imaging and measurement of surface properties at the nanoscale."""@en ;
         skos:prefLabel "CHIPS Metrology: Metrology: Experimental Technique: Scanning_Probe" .


###  http://data.nist.gov/od/dm/chips-metrology/topics/AFM
:AFM rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  skos:Concept ;
         skos:broader :Scanning_Probe ;
         skos:definition """Research topic about a scanning probe technique that
(1) Is used in metrology to measure and characterize surface topography at the nanoscale
(2) Employs a sharp probe that scans the surface of a sample
(3) Provides high-resolution images and quantitative data on surface features."""@en ;
         skos:prefLabel "CHIPS Metrology: Metrology: Experimental Technique: Scanning_Probe: AFM" .


